From e413a2a207fc1b35d84b0f435d7b6a15cb0beb92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:37:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/37] VideoOutput: hand the drawn views to the sink as
 textures, no read back; tell how the frames and the views travelled

The GPU drawer's context is made sharing the scene graph's (the sink's RHI, set from updatePaintNode) when the sink draws with OpenGL, and
the full side by side views leave it as a QHwVideoBuffer of GL textures: RGBA8 for an 8 bit source, the source's own planes (R16, RG16) for
a 10 to 16 bit one. The sink takes them through textureHandle() as it takes the textures of QOpenGLVideoBuffer; a consumer that maps the frame
(the stereo layer's presenter, a test) gets a read back, counted. The textures given back wait for the next drawing. Where the sink draws with
another API, shares no context, or QT_MM_DEPTH_COPY_VIEWS asks for it, the views are read back and the log says why.

VideoOutput.stereoDepthRoute says how the decoder's frames (imported, copied and why, memory) and the views (texture, readBack and why, memory)
travel; stereoDepthReadBacks() counts the read backs. The route message of the frames is said when it changes, not for every frame.

Tests: tst_qquickvideostereo depthViewsReachTheSinkAsTextures (a window with a VideoOutput on OpenGL: 8 bit, YUV420P10, P010 and P016
depth frames, the texture route shows the same pixels as the read back and counts none; red when the sink cannot take the texture).

